1 — Create custom objects and relationships

Open Setup → Object Manager.

A. Create Order custom object
	1.	In Object Manager → Create → Custom Object.
	2.	Label: Order
Plural Label: Orders
Object Name (API): Order__c
Record Name: Order Number (Data Type: Auto Number)
Display Format: ORD-{0000}
Starting Number: 1
	3.	Check Allow Reports, Allow Activities, Track Field History (optional), Add Notes & Attachments if you want.
	4.	Save.

Add standard fields to Order

In Order object → Fields & Relationships → New:
	•	Account (Lookup):
	•	Data Type: Lookup Relationship → Related to Account.
	•	Field Label: Account → Required on layout (we’ll make validation to enforce too).
	•	Order Date (Date): default to TODAY? optional.
	•	Status (Picklist): values: Draft, Confirmed, Shipped, Closed. Default: Draft.
	•	Order Total (Currency, 2 decimals): default 0. Read-only via page layout or formula? We’ll update via Flow. Set default 0.
	•	Description (Long Text Area).

Save fields and add to page layout later.

B. Create Order Item custom object (detail)
	1.	Object Manager → Create → Custom Object.
	2.	Label: Order Item
Plural Label: Order Items
Object Name: Order_Item__c
Record Name: Order Item Name (Text) — or Auto Number if you prefer.
	3.	Important: We will create a Master-Detail to Order so totals are rolled up reliably.
	4.	Save.

Add fields to Order Item

In Order Item → Fields & Relationships → New:
	•	Order (Master-Detail Relationship) → Related to Order.
	•	This will create the parent-child. Label: Order.
	•	Product Name (Text 255)
	•	Unit Price (Currency, 2 decimals)
	•	Quantity (Number, 0 decimals or allow decimals if needed)
	•	Line Total (Formula, Currency): Unit_Price_c * Quantity_c (set formula return currency).
	•	Notes (Long Text Area)

Save.

Important: Make sure Master-Detail behavior sets sharing/visibility as you expect (in master-detail child inherits sharing from parent).

