5 — Automations (Flows) — roll-up and email

We’ll use Flows (Lightning Flow) — preferred over Process Builder.

Open Setup → Flow → New Flow → Choose Record-Triggered Flow (for Order Item).

Flow A — Roll-up Order Total when Order Item is created/updated/deleted

We need to handle Create, Update, and Delete. There are two approaches:
	•	Option 1 (easier): After-save record-triggered flow on Order Item that recalculates total by querying all Order Items for parent Order.
	•	Option 2 (advanced): Use Declarative Lookup Rollup Summary (DLRS) package; but we’ll do Option 1.

Create Record-Triggered Flow (Order Item — after-save)
	1.	Flow Type: Record-Triggered Flow.
	2.	Object: Order Item (Order_Item__c).
	3.	Trigger: When: A record is created or updated. Run: After the record is saved.
	4.	Entry Conditions: None (we want to run whenever quantity/price changes).
	5.	Optimize For: Actions and Related Records (default).
	6.	Click Done.

Flow logic:
	•	Get Records element:
	•	Get all Order_Item_c records where Orderc = {!$Record.Order_c}.
	•	Sort not required. Get All Records.
	•	Assignment or Loop: Loop through the order item records and sum Line_Total_c (or compute Unit_Pricec * Quantity_c).
	•	Create variable varTotal default 0 (Number).
	•	In loop: varTotal = varTotal + CurrentItem.Line_Total__c.
	•	After loop, Update Records:
	•	Update the parent Order record where Id = {!$Record.Order_c} and set Order_Total_c = varTotal.
	•	Save & Activate flow.

Note (Delete case): After-delete flows are available. To cover deletions, create a second Record-Triggered Flow with trigger A record is deleted (before-save isn’t allowed for delete), that uses the $Record_Prior.Orderc? Actually for deletes, set object Order_Itemc trigger A record is deleted (after delete) and then query remaining Order Items for the parent Order (Order Id available in $Record.Order_c in after-delete) and recompute total. Create that as well.

(If this is too much for now, you can handle deletes manually or create a scheduled flow to reconcile totals nightly.)

Flow B — Email when Order Status becomes Confirmed

Create Record-Triggered Flow on Order (Order__c).
	1.	Trigger: When a record is updated.
	2.	Entry Condition: Status__c Equals Confirmed.
	3.	Configure Start: Run the flow After the record is saved and set it to Only run when a record is updated and meets the condition requirements (so it triggers only when changed to Confirmed).
	4.	Actions: Send Email action or create Email Alert + Action. Simpler: Use Send Email core action:
	•	To: Account Owner’s Email: You can Get Records to fetch the Account (Get Account where Id = {!$Record.Account__c}) and then use Account.Owner.Email or directly use {!$Record.Account__r.Owner.Email} if reference available.
	•	Subject: Order {!$Record.Order_Number__c} Confirmed
	•	Body: Include Order number, total, link to record: https://<yourdomain>.lightning.force.com/{!$Record.Id} — avoid hardcoding domain; you can include the record id and the user will open it in Salesforce.
	5.	Save & Activate.

